<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Template for the inert-landing LaunchAgent (ADR-0038 part 2a). Install with
     scripts/install-inert-landing-launchd.sh, which substitutes __REPO_ROOT__ and __HOME__
     and writes ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.devon.inert-landing.plist.

     No secrets live here: the wrapper fetches the read-scoped change-manager bearer and the
     orchestrator's system bearer from BWS at runtime, and the GitHub token from `gh auth token`.

     HOURLY, AND NOT IN A CHANGE WINDOW. That is the setting worth arguing about, because the
     sibling estate-landing agent runs four times a night inside one. Its pass ends in something
     changing a running service; the defining property of THIS lane's population is that landing
     there changes nothing already serving, so there is no window and no hour is better than
     another. Hourly rather than less often because freshness is required: a landing puts every
     sibling pull request behind its base, so at most one lands per repository per pass and the
     pass rate is the drain rate. It is still strictly slower than the GitHub Actions cascade it
     replaces, which merged the moment the required checks went green.

     StartCalendarInterval with only a Minute fires every hour at :35 local. The minute is chosen
     to sit away from the other lanes, whose fixed times cluster at :05, :15 and :50.

     THE PASS IS BOUNDED BY THE ORCHESTRATOR, not by this schedule. Every term is composed there,
     inside the transaction that acts, and the lane refuses everything until
     ORCHESTRATOR_INERT_LANDING_ENABLED is true in production.

     RunAtLoad is false. There is nothing to catch up on, and a pass at login would run at an
     hour nobody chose.

     The exit code is the report. launchd discards it, so the dead-man switch the wrapper arms is
     what reaches anybody — and the log is what says which of the four codes it was. 0 clean,
     1 the tool failed, 2 it could not use its inputs, 3 a pull request is held on a condition
     somebody has to act on. -->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.devon.inert-landing</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>__REPO_ROOT__/scripts/run-inert-landing.sh</string>
        <!-- The wrapper does NOT force this. A bare run reports and asks for nothing, so the one
             invocation that can cause a landing is the scheduled one, and it says so here. -->
        <string>--submit</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>__HOME__</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/inert-landing.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/inert-landing.log</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
